    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always felt like a distant subject to me. Since school, I found it rigid and overly abstract. My grades were never my strength, and I preferred subjects like art or chemistry where I could see real-world connections. Now, as a working woman, I avoid complex calculations unless absolutely necessary. It's not a hatred, but a clear sense of discomfort when numbers become unmanageable.",
